From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro integration
Subject: [PATCH] filter: allow Xiaomi IPA parent and owned rmnet links

The downstream Xiaomi kernel exposes its IPA parent as the virtual netdevice
rmnet_ipa0.  OpenWrt reports that port explicitly with the qcom-soc UID, but
the generic virtual-device filter rejects it before the qcom-soc plugin can
apply its IPA handling.

Allow only this exact parent and rmnet links explicitly reported with the
qcom-soc UID. Other virtual devices keep the upstream filtering behaviour.

--- a/src/mm-filter.c
+++ b/src/mm-filter.c
@@ -230,6 +230,19 @@ mm_filter_port (MMFilter        *self,
         return TRUE;
     }
 
+    /* Xiaomi's downstream IPA parent and its dynamically created rmnet links
+     * are real modem data endpoints exposed as virtual netdevices.  Data
+     * links are admitted only when xm14pro-cellular explicitly assigns them
+     * to the existing qcom-soc device. */
+    if ((g_strcmp0 (subsystem, "net") == 0) &&
+        ((g_strcmp0 (name, "rmnet_ipa0") == 0) ||
+         ((g_str_has_prefix (name, "rmnet_data") ||
+           g_str_has_prefix (name, "qmapmux")) &&
+          (g_strcmp0 (mm_kernel_device_get_physdev_uid (port), "qcom-soc") == 0)))) {
+        mm_obj_dbg (self, "(%s/%s) port allowed: downstream IPA data endpoint", subsystem, name);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+
     /* If this is a virtual device, don't allow it */
     if ((self->priv->enabled_rules & MM_FILTER_RULE_VIRTUAL) &&
         (!mm_kernel_device_get_physdev_sysfs_path (port))) {
